# Frontend UI: Tech + Liquid Glass

**Skill:** Read and follow `design-taste-frontend` before any UI work.

## Design Read (Jarvis)

*"Reading this as: desktop knowledge-hub product UI for power users, with dark-tech + Apple liquid-glass language, leaning toward Tailwind v4 + Motion + frosted-glass panels."*

## Dials (override baseline)

- `DESIGN_VARIANCE: 7`
- `MOTION_INTENSITY: 6`
- `VISUAL_DENSITY: 5` (data-dense app, not landing page)

## Visual Language

- **Dark tech base:** zinc/slate neutrals, single cool accent (electric blue or cyan).
- **Liquid glass panels:** `backdrop-filter` + inner border (`border-white/10`) + inset highlight. Label as web approximation, not official Apple API.
- **Fallbacks:** solid fill under `prefers-reduced-transparency`; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **No AI-slop:** no purple mesh gradients, no three equal feature cards, no Inter-by-default.

## Product UI (not marketing)

This is a Tauri desktop app (Chat, Library, Settings). Apply taste-skill density/motion rules to components, sidebars, cards, and modals — not landing-page hero patterns.

## Pre-flight (UI PRs)

- Dark + light modes tested
- Glass panels have contrast fallback
- Interactive states: loading, empty, error
- WCAG AA contrast on CTAs and forms
